\begin_layout Subsection
The Project Explorer
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In the Project Explorer files can be managed and stored.
 The context menu offers several actions to import and export files for the available Bio7 editors and specialized actions dependant on the selected filetype.
 All the files are managed by projects which can have folders and subfolders,
 etc.
 for managing a large amount of different files.
 These projects and their files can be exported or imported as *.zip files for data exchange.
 The file navigator (
\series bold
Project Explorer
\series default
 view) of Bio7 allows you to create different editor files with a help of a file wizard.
 A double-click on the file in the file navigator will open the file in the default registered editor.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\series bold
Paste Clipboard as File...
\series default
 (context menu, Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+V in the Project Explorer) creates a new file from the text of the clipboard (e.g., an R script or an ImageJ macro copied from a web page) in the selected project or folder. The type of the code is detected (R, ImageJ macro, Java, BeanShell, Python, Groovy, JavaScript, R Markdown, Markdown, Sweave, LaTeX, HTML or text) and gives the extension of the suggested file name, which can be changed. The file is opened in its editor.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
The Editor Area
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The editor area is the area where all files are opened and edited.
 The context menu varies depending on which file is opened.
 When opened the text based editors offer typical text functionalities like:
 Copy,
 Paste,
 Undo,
 Redo,
 Cut,
 Find/Replace,
 Print,
 etc.
 in the context menu and in the edit menu (menubar) of Bio7.
 When a file has been opened editor specific buttons will be added to the toolbar which execute an editor action according to the opened file (compilation respectively interpreting code of Java,
 BeanShell,
 Groovy,
 Python,
 R or execution of a Flow!).
 The editor area can be enabled in every perspective with the 
\series bold
\noun on
Window
\noun default
\SpecialChar menuseparator

\noun on
Show/Hide Editor
\series default
\noun default
 action in the main Bio7 menu.
\end_layout

