\begin_layout Subsubsection
ImageJ Plugins and Macro Paths
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Bio7 supports plugins and macros for ImageJ. The default folders are:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bio7/plugins/com.eco.bio7.image_x.x.x/plugins
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bio7/plugins/com.eco.bio7.image_x.x.x/macros
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Plugins which are copied into the plugins folder extend the menu 
\series bold
Plugins
\series default
 with submenus. 
\series bold
Plugins > Utilities > Control Panel
\series default
 displays all installed plugins. The 
\series bold
SWTImageJ LLM Assistant
\series default
 (a plugin which connects SWTImageJ with OpenAI compatible language models, e.g., of OpenAI, LM Studio or Ollama) is installed by default. Its window can be docked as a custom view of Bio7 and its code tools mark errors, warnings and infos in the editors of Bio7 (a quick fix is applied with a double-click on the marked text).
\end_layout

