\begin_layout Subsection
Image Analysis with R or Python (the R/Python Switch)
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "subsec:R-Python-Switch"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The image analysis views 
\series bold
Image-Methods
\series default
 and 
\series bold
Geometry Selections
\series default
 work with R or with Python. The language is selected with the two radio buttons 
\series bold
R
\series default
 and 
\series bold
Python
\series default
 in the toolbar of the Image-Methods view or of the Geometry Selections view. A switch in one view switches the other view, too, and the choice is kept for the next start of Bio7. With the switch:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
the icons of the views and of their buttons change to the R or the Python icon, the groups are named 
\series bold
Transfer Selected Data To R
\series default
 (
\series bold
To Python
\series default
) and 
\series bold
Transfer Image Data From and To R
\series default
 (
\series bold
From and To Python
\series default
);
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
the Python-Shell view and the Python Packages view are opened instead of the R-Shell view and the Packages view of R (with the option 
\series bold
Image-Methods: the switch R/Python closes the views of the other language
\series default
 of the Python preferences the views of the other language are closed);
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
the actions transfer the data to the workspace of the selected language and the analyses run in R or in Python.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The actions of the Image-Methods view in Python (the names of the created Python objects):
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
IJ RT:
\series default
 the ImageJ results table as the pandas DataFrame 
\family typewriter
IJResultsTable
\family default
.
