\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
ROI:
\series default
 Transfers the x, y coordinates of the current selection (ROI) to R.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Particles:
\series default
 Opens the Analyze Particles dialog of ImageJ, the results of the particle analysis are transferred to R as a dataframe.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Pixel:
\series default
 Transfers the selected pixels (freehand, rectangle, etc.) of one or several images with or without a signature as a matrix to R.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Measure RM:
\series default
 Measures each selection of the ROI Manager (the selected ones, else all) in the current image (of a stack the current slice) with the measurements of ImageJ and transfers the table 
\family typewriter
RoiMeasurements
\family default
 to R (one row per selection): the name of the selection (ROI), its group, area, mean, standard deviation, median, minimum, maximum, integrated density, centroid, perimeter, the shape descriptors (circularity, aspect ratio, roundness, solidity) and the Feret diameters in the units of the image, and 
\family typewriter
imageSizeX
\family default
, 
\family typewriter
imageSizeY
\family default
. The results table of ImageJ and the selection of the image are not changed. The coordinates of the selections are transferred in the Geometry Selections view.
\end_layout

