\begin_layout Standard
The toolbar of the Space view contains the actions 
\series bold
Reset View
\series default
 with the menu of the action, 
\series bold
Clear Measurements
\series default
 (the colors and numbers of measured objects and the picked points) and - if enabled for a plot - 
\series bold
Export Plot (WebGL, Blender)
\series default
 (see 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "subsec:Export-Plots"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

). 
\series bold
Reset View
\series default
 resets all settings of the 3D view to the defaults of the first start (the camera, the grids, the axes, the lights, the colors, the step rate, the height map and the clipping): the loaded data stay. 
\series bold
Remove All Data...
\series default
 in the menu of the action removes the iso surface (with its edits), the volume, the texture and the height map, the model, the plot, the compiled OpenGL model and the measurements: the settings stay.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In addition to the keys of the table: Cmd/Ctrl+Z undoes and Shift+Cmd/Ctrl+Z (or Ctrl+Y) redoes the removal of the surface (also with 
\series bold
Edit > Undo
\series default
 and 
\series bold
Edit > Redo
\series default
), Delete or Backspace deletes the active point of the selected measurement (with Shift the whole measurement), Escape switches a measure tool off and Alt (Option) or the space key with a drag rotates the view while a tool is active.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Custom OpenGL Code
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Custom OpenGL commands can be written in the Java editor as regular Java code. With the Bio7 wizard a new OpenGL file can be created. Two parameterized methods (
\family typewriter
setup
\family default
, 
\family typewriter
run
\family default
) are created which make the gl (glu, glut) context available to draw custom shapes and develop models in a 3-dimensional space. After the compilation the execution is enabled in the 
\series bold
Time
\series default
 tab of the Options Space view.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Float table
placement H
alignment document
wide false
sideways false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "basicstyle={\rmfamily},language=Java,numbers=left"
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
public void setup(GL2 gl, GLU glu, GLUT glut) {
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    // Please enter your Java OpenGL setup code here
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
}
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
public void run(GL2 gl, GLU glu, GLUT glut) {
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    // Please enter your Java OpenGL code here
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
}
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Classbody Java OpenGL
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Since OpenGL is single-threaded the run method is executed from the internal OpenGL display method of the 3D view. TextRenderer objects, textures and models should be created in the setup method with the current OpenGL context (the setup method is invoked again, e.g., after a switch to the fullscreen mode). Several examples demonstrate the use of OpenGL in Bio7.
\end_layout

