\begin_layout Standard
After the compilation of custom OpenGL code the execution is enabled with 
\series bold
Play/Pause
\series default
 in the Time tab. The run method is invoked by the OpenGL timer. The 
\series bold
S
\series default
 button invokes the setup method of the compiled class. The speed of a simulation can be controlled with the method 
\family typewriter
canStep()
\family default
 which returns true with the speed of the slider 
\series bold
Speed (canStep)
\series default
 (in steps per second). 
\series bold
No step
\series default
 sets canStep() to false (a pause). 
\series bold
Show step fps
\series default
 and 
\series bold
Show fps
\series default
 display the frame rates in the view. With 
\series bold
Fixed fps
\series default
 the rendering speed is limited to the selected frame rate (else the default of 60 fps). 
\series bold
Newest OpenGL profile
\series default
 uses the newest OpenGL compatibility profile of the system (e.g., OpenGL 4 on Windows and Linux, OpenGL 2.1 on macOS).
\end_layout

