\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Enable Walkthrough
\series default
 moves the camera with the arrow keys (Ctrl: sideways) in the x, z plane. With 
\series bold
Enable Flythrough
\series default
 the camera moves up and down in the view direction, too. The horizontal and vertical speed is set with the sliders. 
\series bold
Split View
\series default
 shows a second camera in the bottom left corner of the view (the 
\series bold
Position
\series default
 and the 
\series bold
Look At
\series default
 coordinates can be set and stored). 
\series bold
Custom Camera
\series default
 uses the coordinates of a custom camera (e.g., set by a script with 
\family typewriter
SpatialCamera.setCustomCamera
\family default
). 
\series bold
Stereo
\series default
 enables an anaglyph stereo view (red/cyan glasses).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The groups of the Camera tab: 
\series bold
Walkthrough
\series default
 (
\series bold
Horizontal Speed
\series default
, 
\series bold
Vertical Speed
\series default
), 
\series bold
Main View Camera
\series default
, 
\series bold
Split View
\series default
, 
\series bold
Custom Camera
\series default
 and 
\series bold
Camera Modes
\series default
 (
\series bold
Custom Camera
\series default
, 
\series bold
Stereo
\series default
). With 
\series bold
Main View Camera
\series default
 the main view shows the scene from a fixed 
\series bold
Position
\series default
 and 
\series bold
Look At
\series default
 (x, y, z) instead of the camera of the mouse. 
\series bold
From Current View
\series default
 takes the coordinates of the current view, 
\series bold
From Walk/Flythrough
\series default
 the coordinates of the walk camera and 
\series bold
Store
\series default
 stores the coordinates. With 
\series bold
Walkthrough Coordinates
\series default
 a camera follows the walk camera (e.g., a camera behind an agent of a model). The Split View and the Custom Camera group have the same fields; the custom camera is displayed 
\series bold
In Main View
\series default
 or 
\series bold
In Split View
\series default
. The cameras can also be set by a script (see 
