\begin_layout Standard
The Measure tab measures the iso surface and the volume (the figures show the stack Fly Brain of the ImageJ samples, loaded in the tab Iso Surface). The results are displayed in sheets of the Bio7 table: the rows of a sheet and the measurements in the 3D view select each other (a click on a row highlights the measurement, a click on a measurement selects its row). Closing a sheet removes its measurements, 
\series bold
Delete Rows
\series default
 or the Delete key in the sheets 3D Points and 3D Areas remove the measurements of the rows.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Min. Object Size, Max. Object Size (Voxels):
\series default
 the objects with fewer voxels (e.g., noise) or more voxels are not measured (0: all sizes).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Measurement Resolution:
\series default
 1x measures the voxels of the stack, 2x to 4x a finer surface (more precise for small objects, slower).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Decimals of the Tables:
\series default
 the decimals of the values in the sheets (or full precision).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
