\begin_layout Standard
The Default Layers tab enables and disables the layers of the globe and blends them with an opacity (the sliders). Some layers are enabled by default, other layers can be enabled when needed:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Stars
\series default
, 
\series bold
Atmosphere
\series default
 and the 
\series bold
NASA Blue Marble Image
\series default
 (included in WorldWind, also available offline).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Blue Marble (WMS) 2004
\series default
 (NASA GIBS) and 
\series bold
Sentinel-2 cloudless 2016
\series default
 (EOX, Copernicus Sentinel data): satellite images of the earth.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Bing Imagery
\series default
, 
\series bold
USGS NAIP Plus
\series default
 and 
\series bold
USGS Urban Area Ortho
\series default
: high resolution aerial images (partly only for the USA).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
OpenStreetMap
\series default
: the standard map of OpenStreetMap as sharp tiles (also on high DPI displays), see the figure below.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Political Boundaries
\series default
 and 
\series bold
Place Names
\series default
: the boundaries of the countries and the populated places of Natural Earth (public domain, bundled with Bio7, drawn as vectors and text). More place names are displayed when the view is closer.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
View Controls
\series default
, 
\series bold
Lat-Lon Graticule
\series default
, 
\series bold
MGRS Graticule
\series default
, 
\series bold
World Map
\series default
, 
\series bold
Scale bar
\series default
 and 
\series bold
Compass
\series default
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The data of the layers have to be cited, e.g., if a screenshot of the globe is published. 
\series bold
Sources and Licenses...
\series default
 opens a dialog with the sources, the licenses and the links of the enabled layers (the source of a layer is shown as the tooltip of the layer, too).
\end_layout

