\begin_layout Section
The R Perspective and Menus
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:The-R-Perspective"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Bio7 embeds R for the statistical analysis of data, images and models: R runs 
\series bold
embedded
\series default
 in the process of Bio7 (R 4.3 or later, see 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "subsec:Embedded-R"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

). 
\series bold
Start R
\series default
 in the main toolbar or in the R menu of the R-Shell starts R in the Bio7 console. R can then be used in the R-Shell view, the R editor, the Markdown editor, the Table view, the ImageJ views and with the scripts and the compiler of Bio7. The path to R, the R startup commands and the other settings are in the R preferences (see 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "subsec:Rserve-preferences"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
The R Menu of the R-Shell
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "subsec:R-Menus-in"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The actions of R are in the context menu of the R-Shell view (above LibreOffice): the submenu R (Start R, Interrupt R), Load Workspace and Save Workspace, the submenu Editor (Evaluate Line or Selection, Evaluate Expression, Evaluate Clipboard) and the submenu Data (Get Clipboard Data, Remove All Objects); their shortcuts work in all of Bio7.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Start R:
\series default
 Starts the embedded R (the menu of the toolbar action Start R contains Start R and Interrupt R). R can't be restarted without a restart of Bio7.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Interrupt R:
\series default
 Interrupts the evaluation (embedded R: Terminate and Kill are not available, R runs in the process of Bio7).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Load Workspace, Save Workspace:
\series default
 Loads or saves an R workspace (*.RData).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Evaluate Expression:
\series default
 Opens a dialog to evaluate an R expression, the result is displayed in the console.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Evaluate Line or Selection:
\series default
 Evaluates the selected text or the current line of the R editor and moves to the next line. A line is only evaluated if the expression is complete, else it is collected until the expression is complete (interrupt with the action of the R-Shell view).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Evaluate Clipboard:
\series default
 Evaluates the R script in the clipboard.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Get Clipboard Data:
\series default
 Transfers the data of the clipboard (e.g., cells of a spreadsheet) to the R workspace as the dataframe clip.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Remove All Objects:
\series default
 Removes all objects of the current workspace.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
R Plot Devices
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The plots of R are displayed in Bio7 with the device selected in the R plot preferences (
\series bold
Preferences R > Plot
\series default
, 
\series bold
Use Custom Device
\series default
):
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
SWT Vector Plot (embedded R, default):
\series default
 each plot device is a view (
\series bold
R Plot [n]
\series default
, R icon) with vector graphics. The plot is drawn again in the size of the view when the view is resized. The view opens next to the ImageJ-Canvas view and comes to the current perspective with a new plot.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
ImageJ Plot Canvas (embedded R):
\series default
 the plots are displayed in the ImageJ plot canvas (resizable, HiDPI, locator(), save and copy as an image).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
ImageJ View Display Size, ImageJ Image:
\series default
 the plots are created as images in the size of the ImageJ-Canvas view (or of variables in R) and opened as images in ImageJ.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Image, PDF, SVG, PostScript:
\series default
 file devices.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Plot history
\series default
 (R plot preferences) sets the number of recorded plots of a device (0: no history), which can be browsed in the plot views.
\end_layout

