\begin_layout Section
Custom Perspective, Views and Menus
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:Custom-Perspective"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Bio7 can be extended with own user interfaces in 
\series bold
custom views
\series default
 and with a 
\series bold
custom perspective
\series default
 (
\series bold
Custom
\series default
 in the perspective bar) for special tasks. In addition all views of the application can be used to lay out the custom perspective.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Custom Views
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A custom view (class 
\family typewriter
CustomView
\family default
, package 
\family typewriter
com.eco.bio7.collection
\family default
) embeds an own user interface in Bio7: SWT widgets, Draw2d figures, Swing (JPanel) and AWT panels. Several custom views can be created, each view has a unique id (the secondary id of the view) and is displayed in a tab with a title. The content of a custom view can be displayed in the fullscreen mode (F2 the primary monitor, F3 the secondary, F4 the tertiary, F5 a selected monitor, Escape exits).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Float table
placement H
alignment document
wide false
sideways false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "basicstyle={\rmfamily},language=Java,numbers=left"
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
import com.eco.bio7.collection.CustomView;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
import org.eclipse.swt.SWT;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
import org.eclipse.swt.layout.FillLayout;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
import org.eclipse.swt.widgets.*;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
CustomView view = new CustomView("Control Panel");
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Display.getDefault().syncExec(() -> {
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    Composite parent = view.getComposite("panel1");
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    parent.setLayout(new FillLayout());
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    Button button = new Button(parent, SWT.PUSH);
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    button.setText("Start");
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    parent.layout();
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
});
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
A custom view with an SWT button
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
With 
\family typewriter
getDraw2d(id)
\family default
 a Draw2d LightweightSystem is returned (e.g., for the gauges of the Nebula visualization widgets), with 
\family typewriter
setPanel(jpanel, id)
\family default
 a Swing panel is embedded. Further classes extend the custom views:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
DetachableCustomView
\family default
: a custom view which is opened as a detached window, optionally on a selected monitor (
\family typewriter
MonitorChooser
\family default
).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
DetachedControlPanel
\family default
: a floating control panel (a top-level window) which stays visible in all perspectives, e.g., for the controls of a simulation.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
Work.moveViewToPanel(customView, viewId, panel, title)
\family default
: moves a view of Bio7 (e.g., the Console) into a panel of a custom view.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
Work.openPerspective(id)
\family default
, 
\family typewriter
Work.closePerspective(idOrName)
\family default
, 
\family typewriter
Work.openView(id)
\family default
 and 
\family typewriter
Work.closeView(id)
\family default
 open and close perspectives and views from a script.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
The Custom Perspective
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The custom perspective (id 
\family typewriter
com.eco.bio7.CustomPerspective
\family default
) provides places for custom views: a custom view with one of the secondary ids 
\series bold
left
\series default
, 
\series bold
right
\series default
, 
\series bold
subLeftTop
\series default
, 
\series bold
subLeftBottom
\series default
, 
\series bold
subRightTop
\series default
, 
\series bold
subRightBottom
\series default
, 
\series bold
subRightBottomLeft
\series default
 or 
\series bold
subRightBottomRight
\series default
 is placed at this position of the perspective (e.g., left and right are the two halves, the sub ids divide them further). So a complete user interface, e.g., a dashboard of a model or a measurement, can be created with a script. Examples are available in the folder gui of the Bio7 Java examples (e.g., Gauges_4_Views, Gauges_8_Views, FourQuadrantExample and StationsDashboardExample).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Float table
placement H
alignment document
wide false
sideways false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "basicstyle={\rmfamily},language=Java,numbers=left"
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Work.openPerspective("com.eco.bio7.CustomPerspective");
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
CustomView view = new CustomView("Speed");
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
LightweightSystem lws = view.getDraw2d("left"); // the left half of the perspective
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
GaugeFigure gauge = new GaugeFigure();
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
gauge.setRange(0, 220);
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
lws.setContents(gauge);
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

