\begin_layout Subsection
Custom Menus
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Another nice feature of Bio7 is the simple way to extend the Script menus in Bio7 with BeanShell,
 Groovy,
 Python scripts,
 R scripts and ImageJ macros.
 Bio7 recognizes files dropped to special folders automatically and extends the menus with the filename of the dropped files.
 for an overview see (see 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sec:Install-Eclipse,-R,"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Custom Startup 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Groovy scripts can be used to customize the platform directly behind the start of the Bio7 application.
 These scripts will be executed with the Groovy interpreter.
 The scripts have to be placed in a specialized folder (
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sec:Install-Eclipse,-R,"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

) for custom activities like :
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
BeanShell,
 Groovy,
 Python,
 R,
 JavaScript,
 ImageJ customizations or imports at startup.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Open or close a custom perspective or a view.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Execute a startup setup in the different panels.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Invoke an action from the Bio7 platform.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Import libraries.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Start a server application at startup.
\end_layout

